# DataTable

> Lede 0.6.0's docs for DataTable, installed with it. Setup, and every item in the release: [README.md](README.md). Online: https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/data-table.md

A `<table>` with sorting, selection up to every matching row, row links, row actions and paging, plus loading, empty, error and stale states and an optional card layout for narrow containers. `useDataTable` is its model, on TanStack Table behind Lede's own types, for a layout of your own.

## Install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @lede/data-table
```

The command needs Lede's registry in `components.json`, as [README.md](README.md#use-it-in-a-shadcn-project) shows. It also installs the items [`lede-theme`](lede-theme.md), [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md), [`table`](table.md), [`checkbox`](checkbox.md), [`list`](list.md), [`button`](button.md), [`selection-bar`](selection-bar.md) and [`theme-provider`](theme-provider.md), and the npm packages `@tanstack/react-table@^9.3.1`, `@react-aria/live-announcer@^3.5.1` and `@base-ui/react@^1.9.0`. The item's JSON, with each file's source, is https://lede.cloudcompute.com/r/v0.6.0/data-table.json.

